  "title": "Lee-Yang stages and a Krein-space limit",
  "path": "push/c1-leeyang-krein-limit",
  "note": "Rank Gamma_- is lower semicontinuous under bounded weak-* convergence, but in the self-dual conductor normalisation every stage symbol tends to the constant -1 on Re z > 0 for zeta and every unimodular twist, so the chain carries no information. With gamma factor and pole renormalisation the stage has one right-half-plane pole per stage zero (measured), liminf rank infinite. In the strip topology the limit step is Hurwitz plus local boundedness of pole-renormalised Euler stages, which is equivalent to the zero-free statement (von Koch). The Lee-Yang inequality gives a stage bound weaker than t",
  "lesson": "The Lee-Yang stage's index 0 is the inequality Re D_M'/D_M > -(log M)/2, which becomes empty as M grows; the conductor factor that makes stages self-dual erases the limit (symbol -> -1). Any limit step from zero-free product stages is Hurwitz plus local boundedness of pole-renormalised stages, which is RH restated as the PNT error term. r1 holds only at stage level (zero-free stages need the Euler product); the U control fails at the open step, not at a proved one. Primes up to 47 cannot show the convergence mode: the pole factor is within 15 percent of 1 there.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
