  "title": "Sheared Hecke commutator at tau -> 0 with Fricke involution",
  "path": "push/c1-shear-hecke-fricke",
  "note": "[V_n, G_tau] = G_tau(exp(tau l(u+l)/4) - 1)V_n; the eigen-defect order in tau is 1 iff coefficients are completely multiplicative at p, else 0, and no higher order exists. The statement is an identity (multiplicativity at p), not an inequality. w_4 on the X_0(4)(R) arc is u -> -u (evenness only). The sheared prime expansion converges on the critical line only for tau < 0, where the conclusion is false (carry to tau = 0 is heuristic, Rodgers-Tao).",
  "lesson": "The Hecke eigen-property is carried along by the shear (conjugated operators keep it at every tau); the only thing special at tau = 0 is that Hecke operators are translations, which is \"completely multiplicative ordinary Dirichlet series\" restated. Defect order in tau is 0 or 1 and cannot separate zeta from any completely multiplicative control. tau = 0 is the boundary of the sheared prime expansion's convergence domain, approached from the side where the conclusion is false, with l^1 size about exp(1/(4|tau|)).",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
