  ],
  "title": "Joint Hecke-primitive tests in the bridge energy H_c",
  "path": "push/c1-spinor-hecke-primitive",
  "note": "For a finite set S of primes, jointly S-primitive tests are dense (L^2 and Q) in the test class, so the infimum of Q/norm^2 over primitive tests equals the infimum over all tests: the restriction neither helps nor costs. The Gram matrix of dilations does not contain the function's coefficients. All-prime Hecke sums lie in the radical of the zero sum. Referee does not hold the result as written (Lemma 3(a) domain: inverse of M_S does not preserve compact support; 'this is P10 itself' not established).",
  "lesson": "Hecke/Moebius operators are translation multipliers with no zeros in the open strip, so restricting a translation-invariant form (Weil/Q_L) to primitive tests is a congruence and changes nothing; the orthogonalisation step is function-independent. Any multiplicative mechanism must act where the cutoff fails to commute with Hecke (window defect), and that formula is also kernel-independent. Reusable tool: plib.py computes Q_L from primes alone in an orthonormal basis (Loewner form) for zeta and four controls, validated against zero sums to 1e-12.",
  "refereeHolds": false,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
