  "note": "Weight-1 (n4) sum: the exact dual of sum_c w(c) sum_n S(n, l; c) f(n) (Lemma R, classical; confirmed by derivation and to 1e-14) transforms (n, c) only. The twist l <= X^2 that carries A is a parameter, so the ledger map is A -> A; the lattice side has T^(2A-1) terms per l against T spectral terms, never shorter for A > 1. The saving needed is cancellation in l, which no reciprocity on file touches. Variants with a dual family (Motohashi cubic weight, Blomer-Khan level exchange) are recalled, not derived: lengths preserved with positivity lost, or dual family longer; a ledger entry, not a theo",
  "lesson": "Reciprocity identities act on the L-value variable (n or the spectral parameter) and leave the mollifier twist l fixed or turn it into a level; the saving n4 needs is cancellation in l, which none of them touches. Moving to weights that have a dual family replaces Katok-Sarnak positivity by functional-equation positivity, which E_a with real a also satisfies. P2 has an exact anchor B(t_rho) = -1 but no region of absolute convergence in t, so the convexity detector cannot be run.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
