  "lesson": "A rule of the form \"exponent below the seeded controls\" fires on a coherent term that decays (polar term, first moment of theta_6), so the polar and class-mean components must be removed before the fit and that removal pre-registered; here it was chosen after the rule fired. All four sub-items of lead 17 are the same trilinear sum, and at reachable sizes the test resolves exponents only to about 0.01-0.03, far coarser than the Q^(-eta/80) TRO6 needs.",
