  "title": "F_q[T] probe signal on genus 2 and 3 targets",
  "path": "push/c11-ff-genus2-probe-jk",
  "note": "F_q[T] model, squarefree conductors of degree 5 and 7, N <= 3. S_cop(k) is a polynomial in L_1..L_N, the same for genus 2 and 3, linear in Frobenius traces only at N = 1. At N = 1, 0 <= S^2 <= (g/2)(-D.D)/q is Cauchy-Schwarz inside the symmetric block of the graph-class form; ratio anywhere in [0,1], no lower bound. The symmetric block reads only reality of alpha + q/alpha; the Weil bound sits in the antisymmetric block, which the signal does not meet. Registered outcome (b). J_k itself not computed (answer is for S_cop inside the round-8 law).",
  "lesson": "The probe signal and the diagonal class sit in the symmetric (Frobenius plus Verschiebung) part of the graph classes, where the Hodge form reads only reality of alpha + q/alpha. The Weil bound sits in the antisymmetric part, which the signal does not meet. A squared pairing equals a norm only in rank 1 (genus 1). At N = 1 the test is one inequality per L-polynomial, and it was largely decided by c10 4(c) and its referee's correction 5.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
