  "path": "push/c11-rs1-regular-rep-matrix-bridge",
  "note": "Stage A, for the displayed candidates (K), (E), (Q), (H) only. Every bridge object built from M_q lies in commutative C[G] and is a direct sum over characters (Lemma S). The vector 1 is in the cone and is the chi_0 eigenvector, so each cone-quantified statement restricts at v = 1 to a scalar statement about zeta; for (K) and (E) that is H_c^zeta >= 0, which is RH (Lemma P). (Q) at threshold o(1/phi) is a restatement. Entry positivity is character orthogonality and ends at s = 1; the functional-equation matrix has negative entries. Not a theorem that no inequality on M_q exists (cone-preservati",
  "lesson": "Periodicity carried by a finite abelian group representation decomposes with the functional equation character by character, so it adds no inequality. The only extra datum is the cone, and the cone contains the Perron (zeta) direction unconstrained. A CROSS-1 candidate needs a non-commutative or non-decomposing carrier, or a step that reads \"every coefficient matrix is a permutation matrix\" together with the functional equation; E_a and T-NR pass everything else.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
