  "path": "push/c11-rs1-twist-modulus-reciprocity",
  "note": "Stage A. J_p(s;a) = 1 - sum_chi |F(s,chi)A_chi(s) - 1|^2: for X >= p-1 with free weights sup_a J = 1 - #{chi: F(s,chi) = 0} (zero-one law, a restatement). The reciprocity (three-term identity at s = 1, odd characters, distinct odd primes) moves the twist into the modulus but reads only periodicity and the functional equation of the twists; the target's s <-> 1-s is read in 0 steps. T-NR's twisted second moments are a nine-term combination of zeta's at every s, so T-NR passes steps S0 to S4 and its S5 is false at its off-line zeros. Not established: E_a pass for candidate (C), centre statements",
  "lesson": "Twist-modulus reciprocity uses periodicity plus the functional equation of the twists (conductor aspect), which is the 7/8 read set; it never reads the target's s <-> 1-s, so it is not an RS-1 device. Moving l into the modulus reproduces the n4 wall (Moebius signs on moduli, conductor >= length). Any device whose steps are family positivity plus identities linear in Hecke twists is passed by T-NR as a finite Hecke polynomial at q.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
