  "title": "RS-3: de Branges shift positivity and its variants",
  "path": "push/c11-rs3-debranges-positivity-family",
  "note": "Stage A. The entire-function condition implies zeros on the line and cos Delta_h >= 0 at every zero (Delta_h = sum over other zeros of arctan(h/(gamma_n - gamma'))); the weight form implies Delta_h = 0 mod 2 pi at every boundary zero. False for zeta: zero 34 at h = 1 (Conrey-Li, reproduced); weight form fails at the first zeros for h = 1, 0.25, 0.1 (measured). The (a,h) weight family is false for every conclusion half-plane sigma_0 <= 1 relative to Bohr (recalled). V1a = T3 and V2 = G6 are restatements. No Euler-product step. Not established: every-h failure in the entire-function form, tied c",
  "lesson": "Shift-accretivity conditions of de Branges type test bounded imbalance of zeros at a fixed scale at every zero. The Euler product (independence of p^it) is what violates this, so the device runs against R1. Contractivity of the same shift is the classical Hermite-Biehler property and is RH-neutral. Backward heat was not evaluated at the zeta-failing step; no failure at h <= 0.5 was measured below 1e4.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
