  "title": "Bost-Connes crossed product C*(Q/Z) x N^x with Fourier duality",
  "path": "push/c12-bost-connes-crossed-product-duality",
  "note": "Stage A, for three classes of states (sigma-invariant, type I dual extension, archimedean vector Mellin families). Sigma-invariant states factor through commutative C(Z^); vector states with Poisson summation read {L(s,chi)} and the inequality is a square; positive-definiteness of zeta(sigma+it)MF holds for sigma > 1 and fails on 0 < sigma < 1 (zeta(sigma) < 0); Weil's prime side is phi_{1/2}(H_g), a rewriting. T-NR is Tr(D e^{-beta H}) with D >= 1 a positive element of C*(Q/Z) and passes every step. Not covered: other states (e.g. weights on the type II_infinity dual at beta <= 1); no candida",
  "lesson": "Non-commutativity of the carrier is not read by the states that carry positivity: sigma-invariant states see only the commutative algebra C(Z^), and vector states with Poisson summation return the split over Dirichlet characters. T-NR is a bounded inner perturbation of the Bost-Connes dynamics by a positive element of C*(Q/Z), so any device invariant under such perturbations is passed by it. Round 10's reason \"KMS read set is beta > 1\" should read: KMS states exist for every beta > 0 and read finitely many local factors at real beta.",
