  "title": "Control UNIV (joint universality) and the W-adapted cone cell",
  "path": "push/c12-univ-pointwise-control-wcone",
  "note": "(a) Relative to joint/hybrid universality (Matsumoto survey statements): a sup-norm-closed height-independent condition on a fixed window in 1/2 < Re s < 1 for finitely many Dirichlet L-functions that holds off a density-zero set of heights contains every non-vanishing analytic tuple; so such a condition is empty, a zero statement in the same window, or false on positive density. Narrow filter (27 of 34 devices out of scope), not numerically checkable. (b) Cone K_F = {v >= 0, Fv >= 0}: linear functionals are entrywise at x and 1/x; at q = 5 the F-fixed extreme rays give zeta(s)(1 + 5^(1/2-s)) ",
  "lesson": "A height-uniform local inequality on L-values in the open strip carries no arithmetic: it is empty, a zero statement in the same window, or false on a positive density of heights. This filter is narrow, because most devices read the completed function, kernels or coefficients, and its verdicts cannot be cross-checked at computable heights. In cone language, \"automorphism at every prime\" and \"kernel with polar terms non-negative\" separate T-NR and E_a only as inputs; no inequality over a cone consumes the first, since cone inequalities are preserved by every cone endomorphism.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
