  "title": "Hecke/Fricke loading on the real oval of X_0(4)",
  "path": "push/c12-x04-oval-hecke-fricke-loading",
  "note": "Decisive test. On theta restricted to the arc, the summed complex isogenous points of T_{p^2} are dilates of theta; Mellin multiplier C_p = 1 + 1/p - R_p, R_p = 2p^(-3/2)cosh((s-1/2)log p); the relation is the identity c(pm) = c(m). C_p*Lambda is -p^(-3/2) times a T-NR twin. <D_l, W> acts on a W-fixed vector through Dirichlet polynomials; M_{1/2}(Gamma_0(4)) is one-dimensional. Termwise bounds on complex points lose (p-1)p^(-1/2). Second moment over tau+b/p is map row G16. Closed for the four listed forms; not excluded: a functional of unsummed complex points that is neither linear nor a secon",
  "lesson": "Base-side loading on the oval adds no input. Summing the complex isogenous points over b projects onto dilates of theta, so every Hecke statement on the arc is a multiplier times Lambda. A non-commutative Hecke/Fricke algebra acting on a Fricke-fixed vector collapses to its commutative dilation part, and M_{1/2}(Gamma_0(4)) is one-dimensional. The complex-point term is itself a T-NR twin. A device on this arc must read something that E_a and T-NR lack, i.e. the size of the Hecke eigenvalue.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
