  "path": "push/c13-bilinear-reciprocity-height-antibridge",
  "note": "Decisive test. The reciprocity is Voronoi summation for E(z, 1/2+it): the height is a spectral parameter, zeta's functional equation enters only through the gamma kernel, arguments are tied at (s+j, s-j); no kernel in two heights and no Hermitian pair at t != 0. J-form entries (q/pi)^(1/2) Z_chi(t) Z_chi(-t) are real with sign (-1)^(zero count in the window), fixed by the argument principle whether or not zeros are on the line. The only one-sided statement is squares on real characters (identity). Mixed-weight cone statement (Theorem 4(d)) measured on q = 5, 7 only.",
  "lesson": "A bilinear pair L(s,chi)L(s,chi-bar) on the critical line is a point value of a self-dual real function: its sign reads on-line zeros mod 2 and nothing off the line, and positivity of such entries is the property of E_a, not of zeta. The exact reciprocity reads the height as an Eisenstein spectral parameter with arguments tied at integer offsets, so it gives no kernel in two heights and no Hermitian pair at t != 0.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
