  "note": "Stage A. Coefficients are chain products of M(u) = xi(u)/xi(u+1) at u = z+kc, kc-z; in the chamber 0 < Re z < Re c every denominator argument has Re > 1 and strip arguments occur only as numerator zeros (relative to the recalled Garland / Fleig-Kleinschmidt-Persson normalisation, sources not opened). Rank-one Maass-Selberg positivity for all T >= 1 is equivalent to N = z(1-S)/(1+S) being Nevanlinna in z^2 (proved) and is preserved under Blaschke factors over non-real conjugate pairs anywhere in Re z > 0 (proved), so it gives no constraint on numerator zeros. Scope: rank-one proved; closure for",
  "lesson": "Positivity of truncated Eisenstein norms and Langlands-Shahidi non-vanishing act on denominators xi(u+1), which stay at Re >= 1 wherever the mechanism applies; strip arguments are zeros of scattering coefficients, and the inequality is closed under inner (Blaschke) factors. The affine Weyl shift moves the chamber, not the information. Pre-filter for any scattering carrier: does the inequality survive multiplying the coefficient by a Blaschke product over non-real conjugate pairs? T-NR with c>2 is such a product.",
