  "note": "Stage A. At xi(rho) = 0 the completed Rankin-Selberg function has one simple pole pair, but at P = 2 - beta; the gamma pole read by the mechanism is at 1 - beta, so pole minus parameter is 1 for every beta. The vanishing forced there is the trivial zero L(0,chi) = 0 of even chi, an identity for every parameter. The inequality reduces to beta <= 7/4 (vacuous; exponent count reconstructed, paper not opened). Same for Borel Eisenstein data of any rank at regular parameters. Open cell without a candidate: non-Borel Hecke eigen-object with parameter rho, entire twists and pole strictly left of 2 - ",
  "lesson": "Cuspidality enters LRS three times: entire twists, a single Rankin-Selberg pole, and that pole's position P=1 (square-integrability). A zero supplies the single pole but not its position: for Eisenstein data the pole sits at 1 plus the parameter in every rank, and the forced vanishing at the gamma pole is a trivial zero.",
