  "title": "Search for a non-cone sign functional of the theta-normalised kernel separating L-functions from the control battery",
  "path": "push/c13-noncone-kernel-separator-search",
  "note": "Registered question, outcome 'none' (MEASURED, finite search). Dictionary D (minors of orders 2-4 of K(u_i + log n_j); Turan-type expressions, also Hecke-compensated; kernels with and without polar terms; at most 3 real parameters): 12,994,697 functionals x 290 objects; none is one-signed on zeta and the characters q <= 13 and opposite on a battery member of every control class. Of 629,432 functionals one-signed on the positives, 0 reject battery DH and 400 reject backward heat. The positive condition itself does not hold out (held-out L-functions q 14-40 opposite at mean rate 0.287). Lemma H ",
  "lesson": "Sign functionals of the theta-normalised kernel up to order 4 do not separate Euler products from the controls: the character kernels break the Polya-frequency sign pattern more often than E_a, backward heat, EIS-w and theta^w do, so anything one-signed on the L-functions is also one-signed on those classes and on the battery DH function. Backward heat only pushes order-2 expressions further in the direction log-concavity already gives (Lemma H). Total positivity of a local coefficient sequence says nothing about dilation minors of the kernel (T-NR prediction refuted). Float64 is blind where polar terms dominate (about 20% of entries) and gave one wrong sign on a cancelled polar kernel before a noise rule was added; ball arithmetic was needed there.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
