  "note": "Pre-filter and census. Lemma P: T-NR with c > 0 satisfies every hypothesis of type S1 (linear identities), S2 (dilation-invariant convex cone conditions on objects linear in F) and S3 (conditions at primes other than p0); exclusions X1-X5. Device table: 13 of 37 types carry a T-NR record, 0 disagreements. Lemma L: T-NR weights totally positive iff c >= 2. Lemma E: the xi-kernel of E_a inherits every Polya-frequency order. Census of 12 non-cone types: no entry fails both T-NR and E_a at an unconditional input of zeta that another control does not pass; order-4 theta-kernel minors fail both in m",
  "lesson": "T-NR and E_a are separated by complementary kernels: translation-type determinantal conditions on the xi-kernel cannot fail E_a (convolution) and fail T-NR at order 2; theta-kernel conditions of order 1-2 with the constant term cannot fail T-NR (cone) and fail E_a. Total positivity at one prime is ordered against the target: it holds exactly when parameters are real and non-tempered. Low-order minor signs of the theta kernel follow its constant term, so zeta and primitive characters differ.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
