  "title": "Hermite-Biehler position of the Riemann-Siegel half-sum at matched height",
  "path": "push/c3-rs-matched-halfsum-hb",
  "note": "F_N(s) = sum_{n<=N} n^(-s), N = floor(sqrt(t/2pi)), has zeros in Re s > 1/2 at about one per five zeros of Z in every matched window tested (0.17 at 1e4 to 0.215 at 1e12; arb-certified lower bounds 5372, 7260, 8835 in windows of length 1e4 at 1e8, 1e10, 1e12). Smooth cut-off and unequal lengths do not remove them. By the Siegel/Levinson identity the family is the unmollified Levinson method with loss equal to the right-zero count; the mollified pivot is closed row P27. Positive density is measured or certified in finite windows, not proved for all heights. Multiplicativity affects the size of ",
  "lesson": "Any splitting Z = 2 Re f with f a Dirichlet polynomial in the theta frame depends on |a_n| and the functional equation only: by a Gaussian second-moment model the negative-phase fraction is (1-r)/2 with r = c1/sqrt(c0 c2) < 1 (Cauchy-Schwarz), about 6.7% for the sharp cutoff. Multiplicativity never enters; the functional equation only confines the right zeros to within about 2/log N of the line. Close pairs of Z zeros (7 of 8 tested, including Lehmer 7005) carry a right zero of F_N nearby.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
