  "title": "Twin ladder with a prime-built Hermite-Biehler chain (de Branges ordering)",
  "path": "push/c3-twinladder-prime-built-chain",
  "note": "For every X >= 2 and every real symmetric normalisation, Theta_X = E_X^#/E_X has poles in Re s > 1/2 at 1 + 2 pi i k/log p, at 1 and at 3, 5, 7, ...; about T theta(X)/pi lie below height T, so the stage kernel has infinitely many negative squares and no stage de Branges or Pontryagin space or Hamiltonian exists. Adjoining a prime is neither contractive nor expansive; K_X(w,w) is not monotone in X. The negative-square count goes to infinity along the stages and to zero in the limit, which no monotone or semicontinuous device follows. The Euler factor is lossless only about Re s = 0; the functio",
  "lesson": "The de Branges kernel about Re s = 1/2 needs the stage at the reflected point 1 - s, where the Euler product diverges; the functional equation is not an input of any finite stage. Each Euler factor is lossless about Re s = 0 only, and moving the axis to 1/2 turns the Paley-Wiener chain into negative squares one for one (density theta(X)/pi). Zeta's own Theta about 1/2 is a Moebius factor, so its space is rank one with or without RH: the negative-square count goes to infinity along the stages and to zero in the limit, which no monotone or semicontinuous device can follow. Unimodular twists, Liouville, E_a, RZ_b and Beurling fail at the same step as zeta, so the construction does not separate controls.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
