  ],
  "title": "Functional-equation-symmetrised Euler stage with Rouche against the approximate functional equation",
  "path": "push/c4-fe-stage-rouche-crossing",
  "note": "Gonek's stage P_X + chi conj(P_X) has all zeros on the line for any non-vanishing P_X: the on-line property contains no arithmetic. The Rouche (degree) inequality zeta/G_X not in (-inf,0] on a box boundary implies the box is zero-free and is implied (Gonek Thm 5.1) only by zero-freeness at sigma_0 - C loglog t/log X; nothing strictly weaker implies it, and at fixed X it fails at arbitrarily large height (Montgomery, recalled). The boundary quantity log zeta - log P_X - log(1+Theta) is a sum over all zeros; the approximate functional equation re-expresses it. With Fejer weights the k = 0 comb t",
  "lesson": "A stage whose zeros are on the line by construction (functional equation as input) carries no information in that property: it holds for any non-vanishing P, including U. All content sits in the comparison zeta/stage, which at fixed distance from the line is the Hurwitz comparison zeta/P_X (c1 Thm. D), and whose prime-side form is a two-sided bound on the prime tail beyond X at abscissa below 1 (Landau target, twisted local form). The FE term has modulus (t/2pi)^(-d); in the layer d <= 1/L it helps short products (X=2: 0 vs 76 crossings in 2000 units) and lowers the measured margin for X >= 100. Lead 13 is not answered: U fails only at the step that is the conclusion.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
