  ],
  "title": "Hecke operators compressed to the Lax-Phillips space; norm bound on resonance states",
  "path": "push/c4-laxphillips-hecke-compression",
  "note": "On the Eisenstein channel T_p = U(log p) + U(-log p) = 2 cos(log p sqrt(-L)): a function of the wave group, defined for any group. Its compression to K is Z(log p) + Z(log p)^*, of energy norm at most 2 for every inner scattering function; resonance states are not its eigenvectors. For the uncompressed T_p in the weighted-L2 family admissibility of the resonance state already implies the eigenvalue bound; on finite spans a norm bound for all p is equivalent to resonance location; no positive-definite form makes T_2 and T_3 both symmetric on a resonance state. The only inequality obtained is Re",
  "lesson": "On the continuous spectrum of PSL(2,Z)\\H the Hecke operator equals 2 cos(log p sqrt(-L)), so it adds nothing to the Lax-Phillips semigroup; all arithmetic sits inside phi, and the operator framework is identical for every inner function, including non-arithmetic groups and moved resonances. Any Hecke norm bound on resonance states is either implied by admissibility (weighted L2) or equivalent to resonance location. The truncation-Hecke defect lives on the window (a/p, a) and is the automorphic form of closed row G25.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
