  "title": "Ramare / Matomaki-Radziwill factorisation as a source of every-window or one-sided statements",
  "path": "push/c4-ramare-factorisation-pointwise",
  "note": "(i) Bandwidth alpha in (1,2) in the inertia chain needs the Fejer-averaged Hardy-Littlewood error below X^(1/alpha) log X with H = X^(1-1/alpha): a power saving of exponent 1-1/alpha, against proved log-power savings (range H >= X^(8/33) recalled, source not opened). (ii) Outputs are mean squares on Re s = 1; the large-value count at threshold P^-a is T^(2a), against exponent 0 needed at a = 1-sigma to exclude a zero. (iii) Pretentious and log-averaged statements are invariant under finite modification and rotation (tail type), with tolerances (log x)^-A above the size x^(beta-1) of a zero ter",
  "lesson": "The Matomäki-Radziwiłł family is a mean-value device on Re s = 1 whose saving is capped at a power of log (integers without a prime factor in [P,Q] have density about log P/log Q). Its conclusions are closed under linear combination, so DH passes: multiplicativity is essential to the proof, not to the conclusion class. A zero at beta < 1 enters at relative size x^(beta-1), below every tolerance in the family. Add it to the closed families under MV-CAP and tail type.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
