  "title": "Angular family lambda^(6k) over Q(sqrt -3) and ring-class characters as a coherent set of exponent 1/2",
  "path": "push/c5-angular-family-absorption",
  "note": "The transform in the family variable is Fourier inversion on a compact group with no Gauss sum; the root number is +1 (theta inversion; Froehlich-Queyrut recalled), so the Moebius coefficient is mu itself and the rows are Moebius sums of the family. For K <= Y^(1/2-eps) the probe equals its k = 0 row for arbitrary coefficients. The ray coherent set of exponent 1/2 couples s to conj(c) and, with corrected weight N(c*)^(-1/2), does not exceed the Cauchy-Schwarz level: net gain 0, abscissa >= 1 for all K, Y. The model ledger (1+kappa)/2 has its conclusion as input. mu is absorbed only through a n",
  "lesson": "A coherent set of exponent 1/2 is not enough: it must be coherent for every (s, c) pair, as squares are. In a group family (characters injective in the row parameter) the only uncoupled coherent row is the trivial character, which is the Moebius sum itself. mu is absorbed only through a nontrivial weight-1 cocycle of the epsilon factor (Jacobi sums, order >= 3); at order 2 and for characters trivial on a subfield's ideles the cocycle is a root of unity or 1.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
