  "path": "push/c5-device-table-extension",
  "note": "Each device is closed by what it reads. Baker bounds and finite Turan sums read the frequencies log n only (every Dirichlet-series control passes). p-adic/Iwasawa data read zeta at non-positive integers only (the interpolation twin zeta + c L(s,chi_-4) L(s,chi_5) has the same values and a zero at any prescribed point). The tensor squeeze bounds local parameters only (every unimodular twist passes). Carleson/corona criteria assume S bounded, which is RH. The strip Dirichlet-to-Neumann identity holds for DH with its pole sum; the positive prime-side term is a vanishing fraction of the mean phase",
  "lesson": "Before work, ask what a device reads: frequencies only (coefficient-blind), discrete special values (passed by the interpolation twin), size of local parameters (passed by every unimodular twist), or the zero set itself (identity that holds for DH). Only the additive-against-multiplicative pairing fails both DH and the sign twists at non-identity steps, and that pairing is Vinogradov-Korobov, capped because log|zeta(1+it)| is unbounded. Device (b) is closed by argument, not proof; Turan's equivalence and other classical statements were cited from memory.",
