  "title": "Degree-2 positive forms in zeta and companions (device map-open-9)",
  "path": "push/c6-quadratic-companion-positivity",
  "note": "Degree-2 positive forms split into three classes. Log-level squares are linear in -L'/L and lie in the P25 cone. Products of two log-level forms are non-negative at n = pq only if both factors are already admissible linear forms (Lemma Q; with companions relative to a cited Sato-Tate joint density). Coefficient squares sum |b(n)|^2 n^-s are non-negative for every sequence, invariant under every unimodular twist, and non-negative for DH (exact). For b = lambda_Pi the series is L(s, Pi x Pi~) H(s) and its Landau abscissa is fixed by the leading pole for every zero configuration: the device reach",
  "lesson": "A coefficient square |b(n)|^2 is positive without any multiplicativity and is blind to unimodular twists (THIN included). Multiplicativity enters only through factorising the series into L-functions, and at the leading pole every factor is evaluated on Re s >= 1. So quadratic coefficient positivity cannot see inside the strip, and DH passes everything except the factorisation.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
