  "note": "A covariant square of Q_L is a Hilbert-Polya space, so sub-selection defeats every counting test. Fixed Hecke rules: no GL_2 cusp form has lambda_p = psi(p^(-it)) for continuous psi, nor P(lambda_p) = p^(-it), deg P <= 4 (Theorem H2; proved as written for trivial nebentypus; one referee); the eigencharacter of a zero is that of E(., 1/2 + i gamma) in the continuous spectrum. Casimir class: Weyl laws R^2 or R^3, never T log T. Compact at infinity: rank one closed; rank >= 2 without a Hecke rule open and carries no R1. Non-L^2 rank-one family: F(gamma_n) not constant, Euler-blind. The free Borel",
  "lesson": "A covariant square of Q_L is a Hilbert-Polya space, so sub-selection defeats every counting test; only exact tests decide (multiplicity one with Rankin-Selberg, or a single ordinate missing from the spectrum). Every fixed Hecke rule fails because the eigencharacter of a zero is that of E(.,1/2+i gamma) in the continuous spectrum. These no-gos are properties of the automorphic target and hold for all controls alike, so they give no R3. Check push/ for an existing lane before treating a STRATEGY lead as never run.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
