  "path": "push/c8-liou-row-bound-theorem",
  "note": "Liouville rows in one class mod 72, Gaussian row weight: N = D + P + Rem exactly, P >= 0 of exact order M^(5/6) X^(1/3) for X^2 >= C M (proved), |Rem| <= C_eps M^(-eps) X^(1+5 eps) relative to a fixed-twist form of Blomer-Goldmakher-Louvel Cor. 1.4 (twist insertion unprinted). So the Liouville analogue of (5.36) fails for 7m/8 < n < 5m/4. The coherent term is a Hermitian form in the weight and is present for non-multiplicative weights: this half carries no R1 and no R4. THIN stops at a bound on Re x < 12b/7 - 15/14 <= 9/14, which contains an unknown zero-free half-plane for twists of zeta_F. O",
  "lesson": "Liouville closes because mu*liou = 1 puts L(x, psi) in the numerator of each dual-frequency series, so a second moment on Re x = 1/2 + eps bounds the remainder. Every other unimodular multiplicative weight, THIN included, has 1/L there and needs a zero-free half-plane for the whole twist family. The coherent term itself is a weight-blind Hermitian form, so this half carries no R1. Taking Re z = 1 + eps in the row Mellin variable makes the frequency sum absolutely convergent and removes c7's truncation losses.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
