  "path": "push/c8-single-row-bridge-crossing",
  "note": "A cubic-theta row is T = L0 D with L0(s) = L(3s - 1/2, psi). The row's reflection axis Re s = 1/2 is Re w = 1 for L0, at distance 1/6 (in s) from L0's own axis Re s = 1/3. The reflection quotient of T about its axis has no pole from a zero of L0 (classical non-vanishing on Re w >= 1); where T(s_rho) != 0 (float fit at eight low zeros, one unweighted row) the zero is a pole of D with reflected real part (5/2 - beta)/3, which restates beta with no sign or rank condition. About Re s = 1/3 the form is H(T) - H(L0) with no sign from the row's functional equation. The target L(s, eta) enters a singl",
  "lesson": "A theta or Eisenstein-type row carries its Euler factor at the edge: its unitary axis is Re w = 1 for the L-function in its coefficients, 1/6 (in s) from that L-function's critical line. Bridges built on single rows land on the right-of-1 side of the R4 wall (Langlands-Shahidi / Sarnak setting). The target L(s, eta) appears only after the sum over rows, never inside one row.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
