  "note": "Five forms: (i) window form = Littlewood's lemma, coefficient side 0 at every stage for every unimodular chain; the bound-state term is a tail invariant bounded from below only; (ii) mean form E + 4 pi delta = log zeta(2 sigma) is the classical density identity; (iii) at fixed stage no continuous functional of the phases separates zeta from U over window positions (Kronecker-Weyl, row Q21); (iv) the Simon-Zlatos difference condition holds for zeta on Re s > 0 and for THIN on Re s > b/2 with THIN's zero at b right of the line; (v) the H^2 point-evaluation step reaches only Re s > sigma_0 + 1/2 ",
  "lesson": "A sum-rule device outputs Lieb-Thirring (density) bounds; to give \"no bound states\" its coefficient side must vanish, and then its limit step is the target. Test any coefficient condition against THIN first: tail-thin sign changes keep every smoothness-in-delay condition while placing a zero right of the line.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
