  "note": "Lemma I (proved): each squarefull stratum is a signed sum, signs mu(d) mu(e), of sublattice sums Phi(j). Proposition E (proved, one direction): a power saving between strata requires some squarefull j != 1 with N(j)^(1/2+eps) |Phi(j)| >= c Q^delta |Phi(1)|. Measured at X = 1e6, 1e7: exponent of |B| / root sum of squares is -0.005 / +0.001 against the pre-registered -0.02, equal to every control within null scatter 0.003. Lead 17 is closed for squarefull stratification only (second same-kind obstruction after e2-tro6-signed-csum-stratified). Open as stand-alone routes: dual form on squarefree n",
  "lesson": "Stratifying rows by squarefull part is inclusion-exclusion over divisibility: it recombines sublattice copies (index of norm up to Q) of the total and has no saving of its own. The assigned L1 ratio has a random-sign control that decays like 1/log Q (fitted exponent about -0.10), so it must be read against that control, not against 0. The estimator is mostly non-polar remainder (split-half correlation 0.14 at 1e6, 0.23 at 1e7), and the statistic is a family mean square that does not sample zero-carrying targets.",
  "refereeHolds": true,
  "aboutZeros": false
 },
